From: TactiQ OS BSP <bsp@tactiqedge.com>
Date: Wed, 17 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: rk3588s-rock-5a: reserve a TPM event log area

CONFIG_MEASURED_BOOT stores a log of the hashes it extends into the TPM
in memory. lib/tpm-v2.c:tcg2_platform_get_log() looks for that area in
three ways, in order: the tpm_event_log_addr/size properties on the TPM
node, the linux,sml-base/sml-size pair, or a memory-region phandle whose
target carries reg. Without any of them it returns -ENODEV: the PCRs are
still extended but nothing records what went into them, which makes the
measurement unverifiable. The phandle form is used here so the area is a
normal reserved-memory node rather than two magic numbers on the device.

Address chosen against the map already established for ramoops (see the
kernel-side patch 0004): ramoops holds 0x18000000..0x180fffff, which sits
above every address the bootloader writes to (highest is ramdisk_addr_r
0x12180000) and below the first region the kernel reserves (0x03ea0000 is
lower, the next are 0xe8ebf000 and CMA at 0xee000000). 0x18100000 is the
next aligned address in that same verified gap.

Size is 64 KiB, matching CONFIG_EFI_TCG2_PROTOCOL_EVENTLOG_SIZE already
set in this build, so both log paths agree on capacity.

no-map is set here, unlike ramoops: U-Boot reaches the area through
map_physmem on a flat mapping, and nothing in U-Boot should allocate over
it. Note this reservation covers the bootloader only. The kernel parses a
different device tree and will treat this area as ordinary RAM until a
matching reservation is added there; the log must be read before that
matters.

This applies on top of 0003, which adds the tpm@0 node.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [TactiQ BSP integration - board-specific
 memory reservation; not intended for mainline submission]
Signed-off-by: TactiQ OS BSP <bsp@tactiqedge.com>
---
diff --git a/arch/arm/dts/rk3588s-rock-5a-u-boot.dtsi b/arch/arm/dts/rk3588s-rock-5a-u-boot.dtsi
index 1f36bc2..c7c965c 100644
--- a/arch/arm/dts/rk3588s-rock-5a-u-boot.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm/dts/rk3588s-rock-5a-u-boot.dtsi
@@ -74,6 +74,7 @@
 		compatible = "tcg,tpm_tis-spi", "infineon,slb9670";
 		reg = <0>;
 		spi-max-frequency = <500000>;
+		memory-region = <&tpm_event_log>;
 	};
 };
 
@@ -100,3 +101,16 @@
 	/delete-property/ regulator-always-on;
 	/delete-property/ regulator-boot-on;
 };
+
+/ {
+	reserved-memory {
+		#address-cells = <2>;
+		#size-cells = <2>;
+		ranges;
+
+		tpm_event_log: tpm-event-log@18100000 {
+			reg = <0x0 0x18100000 0x0 0x00010000>;
+			no-map;
+		};
+	};
+};
